    delphi:hasConfidence "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The geometry is precise, but mature shape alone cannot establish where it formed. The necessary developmental cellular context is too specialized to expect adequate public data." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Reconstruct Callimitra skeletons and developing cells in 3D, testing for six interfaces, triple junctions near 120 degrees and tetrahedral edge angles near 109.47 degrees with direct colocalization at cell boundaries. Development without four-cell contact would refute the asserted necessity." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Modern developmental imaging of Callimitra is likely absent.", "A tetrahedral skeleton can arise from non-cellular geometric processes." .
